  "id": "Compound::DB00800 - Gene::151",
  "verbalization": "Fenoldopam is shown to interact with Adra2c, which participates in Alpha2-adrenergic receptor activity and is subsequently participated in by Adra2b. This suggests a potential link between Fenoldopam and Adra2b through the Alpha2-adrenergic receptor pathway. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, with each path highlighting a different intermediate step—Adra2c in one case and Adra2a in another—both leading to Adra2b. The shared involvement of Alpha2-adrenergic receptor activity across these pathways reinforces the notion that Fenoldopam may modulate Adra2b through this receptor mechanism. The integration of these pathways implies that Fenoldopam could influence Adra2b via a signaling cascade involving the Alpha2-adrenergic receptor, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
